### 2. `OpportunityErpSyncFinalizer.cls`

This DML Finalizer runs at the end of every DML operation handled by TAF. It checks if there are Opportunity IDs to sync. If so, it enqueues the `OpportunityErpSyncJob` exactly once. It ensures no DML is performed within the finalizer.

```apex
public with sharing class OpportunityErpSyncFinalizer {

    /**
     * Called by TAF at the end of a DML operation.
     * 
     * @param sObjectTypes The set of sObject types involved in the DML operation.
     * @param sObjectType  The specific sObject type for which this finalizer is registered.
     */
    public static void execute(Set<SObjectType> sObjectTypes, SObjectType sObjectType) {

        // Check if this operation involved Opportunities
        if (sObjectTypes != null && sObjectTypes.contains(SObjectType.Opportunity)) {

            // Retrieve the collected IDs from the Action class
            Set<Id> oppIds = TA_Opportunity_CollectForErpSync.getOpportunityIdsToSync();

            if (oppIds != null && !oppIds.isEmpty()) {

                // Enqueue the job. 
                // Note: Queueable jobs persist across the transaction for later execution.
                // Adding multiple queueable jobs in one transaction is allowed.
                // The requirement is exactly one job per DML operation.
                // Since this finalizer runs once per DML operation, enqueueing once satisfies the requirement.

                System.enqueueJob(new OpportunityErpSyncJob(oppIds));
            }
        }

        // Note: TAF calls this finalizer for all objects it manages.
        // We guard with the SObjectType check to ensure we only sync Opportunities.
        // Also, finalizers must not perform DML. We only do Queueable.
    }
}
